WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:18.051
Hey youtubers, this week on Arrow Slade Wilson
returned to fulfill a promise he made to Oliver.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.410
But it’s really just the beginning.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:24.090
This episode is really the first in a line
of four episodes that comprise a villains

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.090
arc.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.540
It’s also the beginning of season 2’s
end game.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.680
Meaning every episode until the finale will
take the Oliver Versus Slade story to new

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.680
levels.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.870
Next week is a break but I will be doing a
predictions video so if you’re finding me

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.010
for the first time be sure to subscribe to
get it.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.570
Since there were so many WTF moments in this
episode let’s do our Top 5, then I’ll

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.580
do my favorite quotes and review.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.650
I’ve also got some more details about Grant
Gustin’s cameo as the Flash later this season.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.829
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode.

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:50.829
But here we go.

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:53.760
Number 5 - Businessman Slade meets Oliver’s
family.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.170
The main conceit here is that Slade was planting
bugs all over Oliver’s house, but I loved

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.630
listening to businessman Slade talking to
Moira as if he were a totally normal person.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:07.050
A totally normal person running on mirakuru
and leading a small army of supervillains

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.770
to destroy her family.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.460
More to his campaign contribution.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.860
I think he’s going to embed himself in Queen
Industries via Summer Glau who is still part

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.950
of the story.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.090
Even though he lied about not having a daughter
I think she’s working with him.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.440
She may not know who he really is though.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.330
To be clear about his children Ravager and
Jericho.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:28.720
Oliver mentioned him in a previous episode,
so either Slade thinks they’re dead or they’re

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.140
emotionally dead to him.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.060
So it could have just been a metaphor.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.710
Number 4 - Team Arrow Rolls Into Battle.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.550
There were a lot of other teasers in the roll
out montage, like Roy with the bow.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.920
But when the “party” so to speak started,
it was like being ringside at a Muhammad Ali

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:43.920
fight.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.290
That’s why my favorite lines of dialogue
from the episode came right then.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.539
Oliver’s “What would you like to do now
Mr Wilson” and Slade’s reply, “I hate

00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:51.910
to Break up the Party.”

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:57.140
The big reveal though was what the actual
promise was and Slade’s ally who takes Diggle

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.140
out.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.630
Number 3 - All Hell Breaks looks on the freighter.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.320
I’m considering a lot of the boat scenes
to be part of this, starting the moment Slade

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.840
learns Oliver was responsible for Shado’s
death.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.490
They rebuilt the whole deck of the boat to
shoot the action scene and it looked glorious.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.430
Just a hail of bullets and people jumping
overboard.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.860
My favorite stunt was hands down, Slade reaching
over and grabbing Oliver mid-air as he was

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.069
jumping over the side and yanking him back
on.

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:25.500
I know a little about how stunts are done,
so I could tell they used wires but it looked

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.650
so bad ass.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.799
And it got even crazier after Slade took control
of the boat.

00:02:29.799 --> 00:02:34.189
Number 2 - Oliver and Slade put on the hood
and the mask for the first time.

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:37.959
This is like the birth of their persona’s,
The Arrow and Deathstroke.

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:41.390
If you remember the australian rum they drank
and that Slade brought in present day.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.840
My screen got all fuzzy so I couldn’t tell,
but it seemed like the name of the rum was

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:46.840
Deathstroke.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.150
Somebody feel free to correct me in the comments.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.489
There were some funny moments that follow
like Oliver missing that Lord of The Rings

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:53.569
signal fire shot.

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:56.969
But really it was Slade calling him a brother.

00:02:56.969 --> 00:03:01.370
I still think Oliver is going to try and redeem
Slade by the end of the season.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.640
Even though they’ll spend the next four
episodes trying to kill each other.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.280
And my Number 1 moment - Slade without his
eyepatch watching the mansion.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.090
The first thing that really grabs you is his
eyeless socket.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.640
It’s just haunting.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:17.610
I think it’s just meant to visually show
the hole he has inside his soul right now.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:20.579
Like punishing Oliver will replace what he’s
lost.

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:21.999
Both Shado and the eye.

00:03:21.999 --> 00:03:25.239
That to me was bigger than Slade just peeping
on the Queens.

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:28.900
That just implies he’s going to use the
surveillance to catch them with their pants

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.280
down.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:35.890
Here are a couple bonus moments though - Roy
and Slade’s handshake of the century, Oliver’s

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:40.329
murder dream of Shado, Oliver’s training
montage on the island.

00:03:40.329 --> 00:03:44.030
Just running while shooting and doing something
that looked very similar to the salmon ladders.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.139
I already said a few of my favorite quotes,
but here are a few more.

00:03:47.139 --> 00:03:52.390
“Lucky for me, before all this I had a lot
of practice.”, Slade calling Sara “Blondie”,

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:58.500
“I’m fortunate to have your entire family
here.”, “I have allies too”.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.799
My favorite quote hands down was Felicity’s
“Looks like Oliver Butt Dialed Us.”

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:06.220
She didn’t have much of a presence in the
episode, but they did give her one of the

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.599
best quotes.

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:09.779
My other favorite was Slade’s promise though.

00:04:09.779 --> 00:04:13.810
“You cannot die until you have known complete
despair as I have”.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:18.109
Overall I give the episode a solid A. And
it’s only the appetizer to the main course

00:04:18.109 --> 00:04:19.530
that is the next four episodes.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:23.620
That’s what Arrow has done so well this
season is build the stories in such a way

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:27.390
that they all inform these final episodes.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.970
We should all go back and re-watch season
1 and 2 right now, because think of how the

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.900
context of those stories change now that we
know what’s really been going on since Oliver

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.900
came back to Starling.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.470
Slade has been planning revenge this whole
time.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:43.310
The episode itself really did feel like a
sequel to season 1’s The Odyssey.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:47.781
Remember that episode setup Shado’s storyline
and mirrored a lot of moments with Yao and

00:04:47.781 --> 00:04:49.020
Billy Wintergreen.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.699
High Fives to the production team.

00:04:50.699 --> 00:04:55.810
Seriously, they rebuilt that entire deck for
the major action scene and it looked amazing.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:05:00.139
Mark Guggenheim was behind it and he also
had a big teaser this morning about Episode

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:01.139
20.

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:04.380
He was waiting for a special announcement
to reveal what’s happening, but it’s basically

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.360
Grant Gustin coming back to guest star as
The Flash.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.020
I’m predicting he’ll come out of his coma.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:13.190
He might not have the red suit yet, but he
will have his super powers.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:17.860
I’m guessing he’ll be key to defeating
Slade.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:21.919
We only know the titles of episode up to 18,
and there will be 23 total just like season

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:22.919
1.

00:05:22.919 --> 00:05:24.150
So there’s still so much that’s going
to happen.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.780
I can’t wait to see it.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:28.710
Be sure to subscribe to get all my Arrow and
Flash videos.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:32.229
I’ll be doing another Flash Bonus video
this week and an Arrow Q&amp;A.

00:05:32.229 --> 00:05:36.250
So feel free to ask me anything you want.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:40.500
Right now click here to learn about Arrow
Season 3 and click here for that Q&amp;A Video.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.500
Thanks for watching, see you tonight.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.290
High Fives!

